body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The ternary operator `ALLOWED_PRIMARY_DISPLAY_MODES.has(mode) ? mode : mode` always returns `mode` regardless of whether it is present in `ALLOWED_PRIMARY_DISPLAY_MODES`. This defeats the validation check. It should fallback to a safe default if the mode is not allowed.

```javascript
function normalizePrimaryDisplayMode(input, structuredContentAvailable) {
  const mode = typeof input?.primary_display_mode === 'string'
    ? input.primary_display_mode
    : (structuredContentAvailable ? 'structured_native' : 'fallback_explanation');
  return ALLOWED_PRIMARY_DISPLAY_MODES.has(mode)
    ? mode
    : (structuredContentAvailable ? 'structured_native' : 'fallback_explanation');
}
